each opponent.\\n[+1]: Add {R}{R}.\\n[−3]: Chandra, Torch of Defiance deals 4 damage to target creature.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Whenever you cast a spell, this emblem deals 5 damage to any target."', "[+1]: Scry 1. Saheeli Rai deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\n[−2]: Create a token that's a copy of target artifact or creature you control, except it's an artifact in addition to its other types. That token gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.\\n[−7]: Search your library for up to three artifact cards with different names, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.", '[+1]: Untap target land you control. Until your next turn, it becomes a 5/5 Elemental creature with haste. It\'s still a land.\\n[−3]: Return target permanent card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card."', '[+1]: Until your next turn, up to one target creature gets -3/-0 and its activated abilities can\'t be activated.\\n[−1]: You gain 2 life and draw a card.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Your opponents can\'t untap more than two permanents during their untap steps."', "[+2]: Chandra, Pyrogenius deals 2 damage to each opponent.\\n[−3]: Chandra, Pyrogenius deals 4 damage to target creature.\\n[−10]: Chandra, Pyrogenius deals 6 damage to target player or planeswalker and each creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.", '[+3]: You gain 3 life.\\n[−4]: Reveal the top two cards of your library. Put all land cards from among them onto the battlefield and the rest into your hand.\\n[−12]: Creatures you control get +5/+5 and gain trample until end of turn.', '{1}, Sacrifice an artifact: Put a +1/+1 counter on Syndicate Trafficker. It gains indestructible until end of turn.', '{2}{G}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Servo artifact creature token.\\n{4}{G}, {T}: Create an X/X colorless Construct artifact creature token, where X is the number of creatures you control.', "{2}{G}: Target creature you control can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or less this turn.", '{2}{G}: Wily Bandar gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)', '{2}{R}, Sacrifice Ruinous Gremlin: Destroy target artifact.', '{4}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.', '{B}: Prakhata Pillar-Bug gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', '{G}: Narnam Cobra gains deathtouch until end of turn. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', '{R}: Weldfast Monitor gains menace until end of turn.', "{T}, Discard a card: Up to one target creature can't be blocked this turn.\\nWhenever Key to the City becomes untapped, you may pay {2}. If you do, draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\nCrew 3 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 3 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Sequestered Stash: Mill five cards. Then you may put an artifact card from your graveyard on top of your library.', '{T}: Mill two cards.\\n{2}, Exile Perpetual Timepiece: Shuffle any number of target cards from your graveyard into your library.', '{U}: Dukhara Peafowl gains flying until end of turn.', '{W}: Bastion Mastodon gains vigilance until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"A failure is simply another opportunity for improvement. Just wait until you see what I come up with next."', '"Airships are too confining. If I\'m in the sky, I want to feel the wind in my hair and taste the aether."', '"All of those Consulate safety measures undone with one simple tweak."', '"At last, the infamous Pia Nalaar."\\n—Tezzeret', '"Baral took my family from me back then. I\'d do anything to face him now."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"By order of Consulate Mandate 482, I am required to detain you, citizen."', '"Citizens, do not resist. This is for your safety. Tezzeret bids you to surrender your inventions. Now."', '"Consider this a high alert, people. Permission to destroy on sight. Either we take it down or it\'ll take down the Fair."\\n—Pav, gremlin watch', '"Creation without connection to nature is just manufacture."', '"Don\'t waste my time with trifles. Bring me works of art, and I will make you rich."', '"Every creation carries a piece of its creators. Their knowledge, their dreams, their soul. That is the best part."', '"Everyone starts off making garbage. If you finally make something halfway decent, it\'ll be the best day of your life."\\n—Nehra, inventor', '"For freedom! For fame! For fire!"', '"For years, I studied the aethersphere from afar, but it was not until I touched the aether for myself that I came to know the power contained in the swirling sky."', '"From the first touch, I know exactly what the metal wants to be."', '"Ghirapur\'s gremlin population poses a threat to the infrastructure of the fairgrounds. Threats must be eliminated."\\n—Sram, senior edificer', '"Good morning, children. Please open your aether valves and ignite your gauntlets."\\n—Rakib, Ghirapur schoolteacher', '"I did not think I would understand the cold filigree creatures of this world, but they too are governed by the laws of nature."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"I don\'t know what that is or who it belongs to, but it\'s shiny and I want it."', '"I like that Tezzeret. He has vision the other judges don\'t. He sees the potential in what we\'re making here."\\n—Faiz, inventor', '"I opened my mind to the immensity of the wonders around me. It was only then that I could see the Great Conduit."\\n—Rashmi, aether-seer', '"I\'d just let the monkey have it if I were you. You can make another, but the same can\'t be said of your fingers."\\n—Turni, Greenwheel groundskeeper', '"I\'d stand back if I were you."', '"I\'ve never seen a world where aether weaves through every aspect of nature."', '"If you wish to produce the finest work, you must start with the finest tools."', '"If you\'ve done nothing wrong, you have nothing to fear."\\n—Enforcer-Chief Ranaj', '"Impress me."', '"Inspiration is reciprocal: we all have a responsibility to each other to create."', '"It\'s a multifunctional radial extension system with superlateral, force-amplifying rigging. Of course it will win."', '"It\'s the must-have gift for everyone on your list. Get one for yourself, too!"\\n—Chammi, curio vendor', '"Knock, knock . . . too late."', '"Let me guess. You thought I was dead."', '"Let us never forget the joy that lies at the heart of invention."', '"My creations still can\'t match the dive speed of those floppy-winged mammals. Maybe I should enter one of them in the Fair."\\n—Viprikti, thopterist', '"Nice invention there. Looks real fragile."', '"No, I don\'t believe they have the proper permits for those, but I\'m not going to be the one to ask."\\n—Caru, Consulate warden', '"Nobody asked you to butt in, Jace. But thanks."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Nothing against you. It\'s just that waiting for Consulate clearance was never really my thing."', '"Now that\'s the Chandra I\'ve been waiting to see."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Our creations are more than mere things. They have life in them, little bits of ourselves."\\n—Saheeli Rai', '"Pleasure doing business with you."', '"Shine bright, bolts tight."', '"Show them. Show them how hot your fire can burn."\\n—Liliana Vess, to Chandra Nalaar', '"Step right up! Try your hand! It\'ll thrill the senses and boggle the mind!"', '"That name shall not be spoken."\\n—Baral, Chief of Compliance', '"The Consulate promised that we would all have access to aether. I\'m just keeping them honest."', '"The fires of invention burn in all of us. I fight for the freedom to unleash those flames."\\n—Pia Nalaar', '"The giants follow the flow of aether, and twice a year it leads them through here. Lesson learned. More clearance is needed."\\n—Sram, senior edificer', '"The judges really put them through their paces, but they prevailed. I think they even impressed Head Judge Tezzeret."\\n—Ritika, artificer', '"The little thopters seemed lonely up here, so I thought I\'d join them."', '"The price isn\'t negotiable, but I\'m sure you\'ll agree it\'s fair."', '"The sky isn\'t the limit. It\'s the starting point."', '"There are many reasons we invent, of which survival is not the least."', '"There\'s no reason to buy a new one when I\'ve got the tools to fix the one you\'ve got."\\n—Ripu, repair specialist', '"They don\'t make them like they used to."', '"They say Head Judge Tezzeret will be reviewing every invention at the Fair. I made sure to build something that will stand out."\\n—Jehvani, Vahadar artificer', '"This is just my warm-up."', '"This one\'s for my mom, and this one\'s for me."', '"This research violates Consulate law."', '"To achieve what none have achieved before, one must dare what none have dared before."', '"To invent is to rebel."\\n—Pia Nalaar', '"Too much friction on your bearings, your countersinking is inconsistent, and there are lines in your casting. Dispose of it, and begin again."\\n—Dovin Baan', '"We all began in nature, and nature is where we belong."', '"We meet again, pyromancer."\\n—Baral, Chief of Compliance', '"Welcome, one and all! Right this way! Open your eyes, your ears, and your imaginations to the wonders of the Inventors\' Fair!"', '"When the time comes, let go. Nothing lasts forever."', '"When you have the chance, take it. Laugh, sing, dance. Don\'t allow the night to end."', '"Whoa there. Easy. We\'re just going to take a little detour."', '"You tread upon the land all the time, yet you seem dismayed when it moves to step on you."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"You\'re coming with me."', 'A retreat to nature can inspire even the most jaded inventor.', 'Aether shapes everything on Kaladesh, from the sky to the sea.', 'Aetherborn patrons use any means necessary to secure victory for their protégés.', 'Aetherborn who are unwilling to accept the decomposition of their bodies invent ways to preserve and augment themselves.', 'All she touches turns to well-oiled, delicately calibrated, perfectly balanced gold.', 'All skyships entering or leaving the fairgrounds must pass through the security checkpoint.', "All the aether charts in the world can't compete with the trained eye of a talented scout.", 'All who listen hear their own song, a unique melody played just for them.', 'An aetherborn wastes neither time nor treasure.', "Architects find inspiration in the dragon's beauty of form, while artificers are influenced by the function of its fire.", 'As unpredictable as aether, and just as hard to contain.', "Automaton inspectors ensure that the Consulate's stringent standards for mass production are upheld.", "Baral's spies always have the latest technology.", 'By the time a Consulate sanction becomes official, the renegade quicksmiths have already found a way to circumvent it.', "Citizens are free to do as they wish, within the confines of the Consulate's laws.", 'City officials once sent twenty gleaming automatons to exterminate a nest of gremlins. They soon saw the error of their ways.', 'Connected as artificer and invention, bonded as rider and steed.', "Consulate engineers have developed safe methods of harvesting aether, but renegades aren't always so careful.", "Consulate guards who pursue fleeing renegades into the Cowl often become lost—occasionally permanently—in the city's wildest greenbelt.", 'Consulate-built automatons have a lifetime warranty.', 'Creators live for that moment of inspiration: precious, profound, perfect.', 'Design leads to progress.', 'Do not be so caught up in keeping track of time that you forget to make use of it.', 'Drakes prowl the skies of Kaladesh, waiting for the perfect moment to strike.', 'Driven by an insatiable hunger, gremlins never cease feeding. They can destroy a lifetime of work in just a few moments.', "Dwarves have an instinct for repair, an inherent understanding of how systems work, and a reputation for fearlessness. They're perfect candidates for the Fair's emergency response team.", 'Elegant filigree birds perch along the eleven bridges that cross Canal Dukhara.', "Even now, Shaila's descendants proudly occupy the greenway that she refused to relinquish to the Consulate.", 'Every leaf, tree, and building in Kujar has been placed to achieve maximum harmony, in accordance with the elvish philosophy known as the Great Conduit.', 'Everything has an off switch.', 'Fairgoers were delighted to find that even outside the fairgrounds, Ghirapur was a city of wonders.', 'Free from Consulate regulations, renegade-built automatons push performance to the limit.', 'Ghirapur is a beacon of inspiration, attracting the most brilliant minds on Kaladesh.', 'Graffiti of the "leaking spire" symbol is found wherever the renegades have been.', 'He has "friends" in places both high and low, and all seem to owe him favors.', "He's set to compete in every race at the Fair, and he plans to win them all.", 'If an elf can dream it, a dwarf can build it, and a gremlin can eat it.', "If her vehicle even has a brake, she couldn't tell you which pedal it is.", 'In Embraal, inventor gangs defend their turf with ingenious devices and blunt objects.', 'In Ghirapur, even the lowliest residents live in lavish surroundings.', 'In the moment of truth, it is as though time stands still, and the whale waits, suspended in the sky.', 'Inspiration leads to design.', 'Inspired by the thorns and brambles of the untamed wilds, elvish armor is both beautiful and formidable.', 'Inventors from around the world have come to the Fair hoping their creations will fly, drive, or sail their way to a top prize.', "Inventors have been known to capture gremlins with the intent to release them in a rival's workshop. More often than not, that plan backfires.", 'It glides around the city, a sublime combination of elegance and utility.', 'It powers the dreams of Ghirapur.', 'It sees itself in all of its creations.', 'It shows affection an automaton never could.', "It won't be small forever.", 'It would be unfortunate if the key fell into the wrong hands.', "It'll either crash or win the race. Possibly both.", "It's rare that the Prakhata Club closes its doors. It's also rare that Lord Gonti meets with Consul Kambal. What are the odds the two would occur on the same day?", 'Its collection is vast, yet each ship has a special place in its heart.', 'Janjeet Observatory is open to the public, but access to the adjoining laboratories is restricted.', 'Kaladesh\'s illicit marketplaces are known as "night markets," but if you know who to ask, you can find what you\'re looking for at any time of the day.', "Life inspires technology, which expands life's domain.", "Loyal to a fault, it anticipates its master's every need.", 'Many an inventor has collapsed under the pressure to create a flawless design.', 'Many elves incorporate the beauty of nature into their inventions. Very few capture its savagery.', 'Most came to Ghirapur for the Fair. Gremlins came for the feast.', 'Natural evolution is often at odds with industrial progress.', "Never before have there been so many brilliant minds and wondrous inventions in one place. Denizens from every corner of Kaladesh will flock to the once-in-a-lifetime Inventors' Fair.", 'Next to her designs, life seems like a pale imitation.', 'Not a mote of dust escapes the dutiful cleaners that keep the exclusive Prakhata Club immaculate.', 'One dwarf on a build team ensures competence. All dwarves on the team ensures brilliance.', 'Open hostilities are strictly forbidden at the Inventors\' Fair, but "accidents" still happen.', 'Part feline, part primate, all trouble.', "Pilots take crippled skyships to the Aviaries, trusting Ghirapur's most talented mechanics to get them back into the air.", 'Progress leads to inspiration.', 'Quicksmiths are eager to jump from one project to the next, relying on flashes of inspiration rather than careful research.', "Renegades do some of their best work right under the Consulate's nose.", "Renegades find ever more creative ways to work around the Consulate's aether regulations.", 'Sanctions, mandates, regulations . . . These things mean nothing to the natural world.', 'Short lives lead to forbidden choices.', 'Some display their trophies at the Hall of Mechanists. Others display their talent in the streets of Ghirapur.', 'Some machines refuse to accept their own obsolescence.', 'Some passengers ride without tickets.', 'Some say tales of the Narnam greenhouse are told to scare the children, but every tale grows from a seed of truth.', 'Sometimes the smallest things make the biggest difference.', "Textiles at the Inventors' Fair feature threads from every corner of Kaladesh.", 'The "gifted" among the aetherborn can draw the life essence of other living beings into themselves.', 'The Consulate keeps watch at each of the eleven bridges to ensure that the market remains a haven for commerce, not for con artists.', "The Consulate rarely cracks the coded announcement of a night market's location before dawn, and enforcers are taken care of if they wander too close.", "The Consulate's automaton bank contains only the most impressive specimens.", "The Inventors' Renaissance came on the heels of the Great Aether Boom, hiking demand for raw materials of every kind.", 'The Iron League prides itself on its metal-shaping techniques.', 'The aethersphere is home to the most wondrous beings on all of Kaladesh, although the dangers of traversing it mean that not much is known of them.', "The avant-garde among Ghirapur's inventors disregard the Consulate's safety standards completely.", 'The chasm of years and worlds collapsed under the power of their embrace.', 'The drake flew true. The arrow flew truer.', 'The first tentative flaps are like a song to his soul.', 'The foundries of Kaladesh run like clockwork under the supervision of their formidable overseers.', 'The giant-decorating contest at the migration festival is a tradition that may have started as a dare.', 'The great birds dive through the sky, wings skimming the aether streams, to fall upon their unsuspecting prey.', 'The judges at the Fair are held in such high esteem that a nod of recognition can inspire an inventor for a lifetime—and a wave of dismissal can end a career.', 'The louder the elephant trumpeted, the more the crowd cheered. And the more the crowd cheered . . .', 'The most dangerous thing an artificer can do is believe an invention is perfect.', 'The power of aether draws creatures to it like a magnetic force, and those that are touched by it are forever altered.', "The results of Rashmi's experimentation forced her to consider the possibility that multitudinous realities existed beyond her own.", 'The swarm leaves behind a flawless pattern that only occasionally threatens the structural integrity of the wood.', 'The teeth marks add character.', "There is no dress code for the Inventors' Fair, but you'll be hard-pressed to find anyone or anything not done up in their finest.", "There's so much more to Ghirapur than can be accessed by traditional roads.", 'This detailed model allows the edificers to examine the city from every angle.', 'Those who move harmoniously with the flow of aether can channel the power of the natural world.', 'To understand Kaladesh, one must first understand how aether and invention flow together through the great Aether Cycle.', 'Tonight at the Grand Exhibition, witness Head Judge Tezzeret face off against the infamous renegade Pia Nalaar.', 'Vedalken have six thin, agile fingers on each hand, giving them unparalleled dexterity.', 'Was it just lonely, or was some form of evolution inevitable?', 'Waterways carve their routes through the land to reflect the paths the aether streams cut through the clouds.', "Were she not a judge, she'd win the division herself.", 'When Baral constructed his trap for Chandra, he did not account for the arrival of an enormous leonin wielding a twin-headed axe.', 'Where high society and dark opportunity intersect.', "While most power is used for ordinary, everyday tasks, one shouldn't underestimate its potential for the extraordinary.", "Yesterday's marvels are today's antiques."]
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Ben Maier', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Christine Choi', 'Christopher Burdett', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darek Zabrocki', 'David Gaillet', 'David Palumbo', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Efflam Mercier', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eytan Zana', 'Filip Burburan', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Greg Opalinski', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jakub Kasper', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Kang', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jeff Simpson', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Josh Hass', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Jung Park', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Kirsten Zirngibl', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lindsey Look', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Stewart', 'Mike Bierek', 'Min Yum', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Richard Wright', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Sara Winters', 'Scott Murphy', 'Sean Murray', 'Sean Sevestre', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Sidharth Chaturvedi', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Sung Choi', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Titus Lunter', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tom Babbey', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tommy Arnold', 'Tony Foti', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Viktor Titov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zoltan Boros']
